Policies and practices: underwriting strategy
i) All long-term insurance product additions and alterations are required to pass through the approval framework that forms
part of the life insurance business’ governance process. The statutory actuaries approve the policy conditions and premium
rates of new and revised products;
ii) Specific testing for HIV/Aids is carried out in all cases where the applications for risk cover exceed a set limit. Product pricing
and reserving policies also include specific allowance for the risk of HIV/ Aids;
